# Ideas ledger — evolution summits

Append-only. One entry per idea any persona raises in any summit — this file is
the panel's memory across cycles and the human's readable window into what the
"board" has been thinking about. Every summit READS it before generating (so a
rejected idea is not re-proposed identically). Retrospective coverage rotates on
the structural audit-marker entries written by `evolve.sh log --audit-of NNNN`
— free text merely *mentioning* a task id never counts as coverage.

Entry formats (one line each, written by `evolve.sh log`; the audit marker's
tab-delimited `[audit:#NNNN]` column can only be produced by `--audit-of`):

```
- [YYYY-MM-DD] <persona> — <idea one-liner> — <disposition>
- [YYYY-MM-DD]	[audit:#NNNN]	<persona> — <re-examination> — <disposition>
```

Dispositions: `queued as task #NNNN` · `merged into existing task #NNNN` ·
`rejected by critic: <reason>` · `deferred: <reason>` · and for audit entries,
the retrospective verdict (e.g. `approved as-is` · `expand — queued as task #NNNN`).

